# Workshops that use secrets fill this file in with the keys they need;
# workshops that don't use secrets delete this file. `.gitignore` already
# excludes `.env`, so the actual values never get committed.
#
# Convention: lesson verify scripts load `.env` via
#   `tsx --env-file-if-exists=../../.env src/verify.ts`
# so the file at the workshop root auto-loads for every lesson without
# any per-lesson dotenv plumbing.
#
# AFFORDANCE: ship each key line uncommented with an empty value, like:
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# NOT commented out like `# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...placeholder...`. Two
# reasons:
#
#   1. Learners pasting a real key onto a commented line — without
#      removing the `#` — silently end up with an inert .env. tsx
#      ignores commented lines; the failure mode is an opaque 401 from
#      the API. (Real bug we hit in evals-workshop's first walks.)
#   2. An empty value populates `process.env.KEY = ""`. JS falsy, so
#      workshop code that checks `if (process.env.KEY)` falls through
#      cleanly to whatever fallback you wire (e.g. `lwc env get`) with
#      no warning-log noise.
#
# Authors: tell learners they have TWO setup paths:
#
#   1. Paste their real key after the `=` and save.
#   2. Run `lwc env set <KEY_NAME>` in their terminal — hidden prompt,
#      stored at ~/.lwc/env.json (chmod 600). Workshops that fall back
#      to `lwc env get` pick up the stored value automatically.

# TODO: list this workshop's required secrets below, each as
#   KEY_NAME=
# (uncommented, empty value). Delete this file entirely if your workshop
# doesn't use any secrets.
